      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area once hosted Tojgun Pasha's mosque, later replaced by a Baroque monastery and the Church of Stigmatisation of Saint Francis.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://welovebudapest.com/en/article/2023/09/16/active-discover-vizivaros-one-of-budapest-s-most-astonishing-areas/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The red house on the square’s edge, now the Hungarian Charity Service of the Order of Malta, dates back to the Ottoman era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://welovebudapest.com/en/article/2023/09/16/active-discover-vizivaros-one-of-budapest-s-most-astonishing-areas/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1901 market hall on Fő utca once hosted 690 stalls and later became the Budapest flower market until the 1970s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
